.TH "tangsible-host" "1" "2026-09-05" "Tangsible" "Tangsible Manual"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
tangsible-host - everything Tangsible can determine about one host
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBtangsible host\fR \fIhostname\fR [\fIplaybook.\&yml\fR] [\fIansible-playbook args\fR .\&.\&.\&]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBhost\fR shows all available information about a host from the inventory.\& If
\fIplaybook.\&yml\fR is omitted, it is resolved the same way \fBtangsible-run\fR(1)
resolves one (see \fBtangsible\fR(1)), though a playbook is only strictly
required for the Plays tab; the others work without one.\&
.PP
Standard \fBansible-playbook\fR(1) arguments can be used, e.\&g.\& \fB--inventory\fR or
\fB--tags\fR can be provided.\&
.PP
.SH TABS
.PP
\fBSummary\fR
.RS 4
Live-gathered facts (FQDN, IP addresses, OS, architecture, RAM,
virtualization, and more), fetched from the host.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBGroups\fR
.RS 4
Every inventory group this host belongs to, direct or transitive —
a host-centric view of the group membership in contrast to the
group-centric format of the inventory file.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBPlays\fR
.RS 4
Every play in \fIplaybook.\&yml\fR that would actually run against this
host.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBhost_vars\fR
.RS 4
The host'\&s own \fBhost_vars\fR files, if any are found alongside the
playbook or inventory.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBEverything known\fR
.RS 4
Raw output from \fBansible-inventory --host\fR \fIhostname\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH KEY BINDINGS
.PP
\fBTab / Shift-Tab\fR
.RS 4
Switch tabs.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBUp / Down, Page Up / Down, CTRL-B / F, Home/End, CTRL-A / E\fR
.RS 4
Scroll the active tab.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB/\fR
.RS 4
Search the active tab'\&s text.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBn / N\fR
.RS 4
Jump to the next / previous match when search is active.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBEsc\fR
.RS 4
Close search dialog.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBq / Ctrl-C\fR
.RS 4
Quit.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
\fB0\fR
.RS 4
Normal exit, however the view was closed.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB1\fR
.RS 4
Unable to write the stub playbook to create the Plays tab.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB2\fR
.RS 4
Usage error: no \fIhostname\fR was given.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBtangsible\fR(1), \fBtangsible-hosts\fR(1), \fBtangsible-template\fR(1)
